---
// The two-mode estimation pipeline (paper Fig. 3) as responsive HTML. It lays out as two
// columns on wide screens and stacks on phones, and it follows the page's light/dark theme.
---

<div class="not-prose my-8">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <!-- Mode 1 -->
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-xl border border-sky-300 bg-sky-50 p-5 dark:border-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-950/40">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-sky-700 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-wide text-white">MODE 1</span>
        <h4 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">Low sliding push</h4>
      </div>
      <p class="m-0 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
        Push low enough to slide the object and measure tangential force. The released estimator uses the median force over a steady-sliding window.
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-white px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-sm shadow-sm dark:bg-zinc-900">
        f<sub>t</sub> = μ<sub>t</sub> · m g &nbsp;⇒&nbsp; cache <b>μ<sub>t</sub>·m</b>
      </div>
      <p class="m-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Sliding sees only the product μ<sub>t</sub>·m, so mass and friction can't be separated from it alone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Mode 2 -->
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5 dark:border-amber-800 dark:bg-amber-950/40">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-amber-700 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-wide text-white">MODE 2</span>
        <h4 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">Press-and-pull tipping</h4>
      </div>
      <p class="m-0 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
        Press down above the pivot edge to pin it, then pull along a circular arc about it and back.
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-white px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-sm shadow-sm dark:bg-zinc-900">
        <sup>O</sup>w<sub>app</sub> = −Ad<sup>T</sup><sub>T<sub>SO</sub></sub> <sup>S</sup>w<sub>meas</sub>
        &nbsp;→&nbsp; torque balance &nbsp;⇒&nbsp; <b>(m, z<sub>c</sub>)</b>
      </div>
      <p class="m-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
        The ground wrench acts through the pivot, so the moment balance is independent of μ<sub>t</sub>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- merge arrows -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 text-zinc-400 dark:text-zinc-500" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="flex justify-center py-1 text-2xl">↓</div>
    <div class="flex justify-center py-1 text-2xl">↓</div>
  </div>

  <section class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-300 bg-emerald-50 p-5 text-center dark:border-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-950/40">
    <div class="font-mono text-base">
      μ<sub>t</sub> = (μ<sub>t</sub>·m) / m &nbsp;=&nbsp; |f<sub>t</sub>| / (m g)
    </div>
    <div class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">All recovered: m, z<sub>c</sub>, μ<sub>t</sub></div>
    <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
      Input: planar CoM (x<sub>c</sub>, y<sub>c</sub>) from prior planar-pushing estimation. Output: mass, CoM height, and table friction.
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
